  "actions": [
    {
      "accreditor": "MSCHE",
      "action_type": "other",
      "action_label": "To acknowledge receipt of the complex substantive change request. To include the change in legal status, form of control, or ownership within the institution's scope of accreditation effective July 1, 2026, the anticipated date of the transaction. To note the complex substantive change request includes the merger of New Jersey City University with Kean University, effective July 1, 2026, the anticipated date of the transaction. To note that Kean University is the surviving institution. To note that the surviving institution is responsible for ensuring the submission of all required reports and information on behalf of the integrated institution. To note that New Jersey City University will maintain accreditation for the sole purpose of implementing the teach-out plan and agreements and effectuating the change in ownership process with the United States Department of Education per the United States Department of Education's Updated Guidance and Procedures for Changes in Ownership, dated September 15, 2022 (Electronic Announcement ID: GENERAL-22-70). To note that the accreditation cease date will be determined after the United States Department of Education (USDE) has approved the merger application. To note that the main campus of New Jersey City University at 2039 Kennedy Boulevard, Jersey City, NJ 07305 will become an additional location included within the scope of accreditation of Kean University. To require immediate notification when New Jersey City University becomes an additional location of Kean University by email to [email protected]. To require notification of the date of the closing of the transaction within five calendar days of the transaction, or immediate notification if there is any delay in the anticipated date of the closing of the transaction by email to [email protected]. To note that written documentation of review or approval from the following agencies has been received: the New Jersey Office of the Secretary of Higher Education (OSHE) and the New Jersey State Legislature. To request a complex substantive change supplemental information report, due September 1, 2026, documenting (1) updated status of the implementation of the complex substantive change (Complex Substantive Change Procedures); (2) written evidence of approvals from all necessary licensing, regulatory, or other legal entities as necessary, including the United States Department of Education (Standard II); (3) evidence of formal conflict-of-interest policies and recusal procedures post-merger transition (Standard II); (4) evidence of individualized credit evaluations and teach-out communication provided to New Jersey City University students (Standard II); (5) sufficient learning experiences and resources to support both the institution's programs of study and the academic progress of all student populations (Standard III); (6) evidence of the integration of New Jersey City University athletic, student life, and other extracurricular activities that are regulated by the same academic, fiscal, and administrative principles and procedures that govern all other programs (Standard IV); (7) evidence of the integration of the New Jersey City University Foundation and its disbursement of scholarship funds (Standard IV); (8) assessment of student learning and achievement that demonstrates that students have accomplished educational goals consistent with their programs of study (Standard V); (9) evidence of migration of New Jersey City University data into the Student Success Data Collaborative (Standard V); (10) evidence that its student learning programs are characterized by coherence and appropriate assessment of student achievement throughout its educational offerings, at both institutional and program levels, with evidence that faculty and appropriate institutional stakeholders have considered and used assessment results to improve teaching and learning (Standard V); (11) the institution's updated Eligibility and Certification Approval Report (ECAR) reflecting the inclusion of the additional location (Standard VI); and (12) evidence of the implementation of a unified governance structure (Standard VII) (Fourteenth Edition and Evidence Expectations by Standard Guidelines). To direct a complex substantive change site visit to the additional location at 2039 Kennedy Boulevard Jersey City, NJ 07305, and to the main campus at 1000 Morris Avenue, Union, NJ 07083, as soon as practicable but no later than six months after July 1, 2026 the anticipated date of the transaction. To remind the institution of its obligation to inform the Commission about any and all developments relevant to this action. To note the Commission may rescind this action if any developments reveal additional information that might have affected the Commission's decision, or the complex substantive change is not implemented within one year of this action. To direct the institution to conduct a new comprehensive evaluation in accordance with Commission policy and procedures and federal regulation 34 CFR 602.22(h). The next evaluation visit is scheduled for 2029-2030. To note the Commission action for New Jersey City University on April 23, 2026.",
      "action_label_short": "Merger of New Jersey City University with Kean University (effective July 1, 2026)",
